   ◆ Ada's past: He was a good husband to her, and a kind father to the boys, and, although he died poor, he left her with an unblemished character, and a name that will always be respected.
   ◆ Arthur's past: He was steady and diligent, and proved himself a trustworthy and valuable servant to his employers.  During the ten years he was in their service he never had a holiday, and, except when prevented by illness, was never absent from his post a single morning.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He was a faithful and punctual servant, and never spent a farthing of his own money until he had first set aside something for the benefit of his children.  He never gambled, and was particularly averse to speculation.
